.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BN_SECURITY_BITS 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BN_security_bits
.Nd returns bits of security based on given numbers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bn.h
.Ft int
.Fo BN_security_bits
.Fa "int L"
.Fa "int N"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BN_security_bits
returns the number of bits of security provided by a specific algorithm
and a particular key size.
The bits of security is defined in NIST SP800-57. Currently,
.Fn BN_security_bits
support two types of asymmetric algorithms: the FFC (Finite Field
Cryptography) and IFC (Integer Factorization Cryptography).
For FFC, e.g., DSA and DH, both parameters
.Fa L
and
.Fa N
are used to decide the bits of security, where
.Fa L
is the size of the public key and
.Fa N
is the size of the private key.
For IFC, e.g., RSA, only
.Fa L
is used and it's commonly considered to be the key size (modulus).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Number of security bits.
.Sh NOTES
ECC (Elliptic Curve Cryptography) is not covered by the
.Fn BN_security_bits
function.
The symmetric algorithms are not covered neither.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr DH_security_bits 3 ,
.Xr DSA_security_bits 3 ,
.Xr RSA_security_bits 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn BN_security_bits
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
